  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question17
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 'Intersections of this diagonal line with lines parallel

    to
    AB at A<sub>4</sub>, A<sub>3</sub>, A<sub>2</sub> and A<sub>1</sub> are respectively
    at 0.2

    cm, 0.4 cm, 0.6 cm and 0.8 cm.'
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: 'The diagonal line divides 1 cm into five equal divisions. According
    to the law of proportional similarity,

    for 5 equal divisions, the given
    line will be divided into sections of lengths 0.2 cm. As a result, 0.2 cm is

    the
    least count of the scale in this case.


    Hence the intercepts must be at
    0.2 cm, 0.4 cm, 0.6 cm and 0.8 cm marks, respectively.'
  options:
  - True
  - False
  - Both
  - Neither
  correctOptionIndex: 1
